comments.body:
Thank you for your explaination.

I'm conducting some tests on a simple LAN network with four hosts and a P4 switch configured as L2 switch. I'm using a direct meter on a table that maches the soruce MAC address with the aim of dropping packets marked as red while sending a notifcation to the control plane: 
```
	apply {
		// MAT that notifies the controller to execute l2 learning operation in case of a missmatch
		// A direct meter is applied in case of a match
		learning.apply();
                if (ig_md.meter_color <= 8w2) {
                    if (ig_md.meter_color == 8w1 || ig_md.meter_color == 8w2) {
		        \\ YELLOW PACKET
			\\ Notify the controller without drop the packet
                        send_warning_digest();
		    }    
                    if (dmac.apply().miss) {
                        flooding.apply();
		    }
                } else {
		    \\ RED PACKET
		    \\ Notify the contoller and drop the packet
    		    send_alarm_digest();
                }
                ig_intr_tm_md.bypass_egress = 1w1;
	}
```
I'm using SCAPY to send ICMP packets from one host to another, but sometimes I never get red packets, and other times I see some red packets only when the second host replies. I have configured the following parameters:

- PIR = 20;
- CIR = 10;
- PBS = 20;
- CBS = 10.

The sender host sends about 70-80 pkt/s, so I expect that several packets could be marked as red.

Could you explain me what I am doing wrong?

Thank you for your time.
